{"type":"message","id":"0d4419a0","parentId":"f5b746c9","timestamp":"2026-03-14T14:22:39.935Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see the issue now. The cron job for processing briefs is failing because it's trying to resolve `@:25` as a Telegram chat ID, but that syntax isn't valid — Telegram API requires numeric chat IDs (like `468031863`).\n\nLooking at the existing jobs:\n- There are hourly fetch and process jobs running with similar issues\n- The github-push-sync job is using `to: \"468031863\"` which works for delivery\n- All these jobs have consecutive errors due to the @heartbeat resolution failure\n\nThe core problem:\n1. Telegram's API only accepts numeric chat IDs (e.g., \"468031863\")\n2. The `@:25` syntax is a placeholder that needs to be replaced with an actual numeric ID\n3. Without knowing the real chat ID for channel @:25, we can't resolve it\n\nWhat I need to do:\n- Update the cron job payload to use the correct numeric chat ID\n- Or change delivery mode to \"none\" if this is just a processing task that doesn't need to announce anything\n\nSince this appears to be a processing/analytics task rather than something that needs to send messages, the best approach is to either:\n1. Set `to: null` or remove it from delivery (since we don't have the ID)\n2. Or find out what numeric ID @:25 resolves to\n\nLet me update this job with a proper payload that won't fail on Telegram resolution."},{"type":"text","text":"I see the issue. The cron job is failing because `@:25` isn't a valid Telegram chat ID — Telegram's API requires numeric IDs (like `468031863`). \n\nLooking at your other jobs, they use `to: \"468031863\"` for delivery. Since this appears to be an internal processing task, I'll update it to not require Telegram resolution anymore.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"295781830","name":"cron","arguments":{"action":"update","jobId":"a0036b1a-bb1b-428f-a028-06ab983a1287","patch":{"payload":{"message":"Process and analyze the daily brief content fetched at :10. This runs every hour at :25 to process the previously fetched data.","kind":"agentTurn"}}}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"qwen3-5-9b","model":"qwen3.5-9b-claude-4.6-opus-reasoning-distilled","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773498100677}}
